hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1204","Abu Rashid al-Hubrani said, ""I came to 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar and
asked him to relate to us what he had heard from the Messenger of Allah,
may Allah bless him and grant him peace. He handed me a paper and said,
'This is what the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, wrote
for me.' I looked at it and it read:
'Abu Bakr as-Siddiq asked the Prophet,
may Allah bless him and grant him peace, ""Messenger of Allah, teach me
what to say in the mornings and evenings."" He said, ""Abu Bakr, say, 'O
Allah, the Creator of the heavens and the earth, the Knower of the Unseen
and Visible. the Lord of all things and their Master. I seek refuge with
You from the evil of shaytan and his encouragement to associate and that
I bring evil on myself or bring it on another Muslim.'""'"""
"1205","It is narrated from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that when the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, would rise in the morning, he would supplicate: ""O Allah, by Your favour we have reached the morning, and by Your favour we reach the evening. By Your favour we live and in Your name we die, and to You is the resurrection."" And when he would enter the evening, he would say: ""O Allah, by Your favour we have reached the evening, and by Your favour we reach the morning. By Your favour we live and in Your name we die, and to You is the return.""
Al-Adab al-Mufrad, Hadith: 1205; Arabic Hadith: 1205"
"1206","Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, never used to omit this supplication in the evening and in the morning: ""O Allah, I ask You for well-being in this world and the Next. O Allah, I ask You for pardon and well-being in my religion, my worldly affairs, my family and my wealth. O Allah, veil my weak points and safeguard me from what I fear. O Allah, protect me from in front of me, from behind me, from my right, from my left, and from above me, and I seek refuge in Your greatness from being struck down from beneath me."""
"1207","Anas ibn Malik reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, ""Whoever says when morning comes: 'O Allah, we have entered the morning and the dominion has entered the morning belonging to Allah, and we bear witness to You and to the bearers of Your Throne, and Your angels, and all Your creation, that You are Allah, there is no god but You, alone, without any partner, and that Muhammad, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, is Your slave and Your Messenger' – Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will free a quarter of him from the Fire on that day. Whoever says it twice, Allah will free half of him from the Fire. Whoever says it four times, Allah will free him from the Fire entirely on that day."""
"1208","Sayyiduna Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him) narrates that Sayyiduna Abū Bakr (may Allāh be pleased with him) submitted: ""O Messenger of Allāh! Teach me a supplication that I may recite in the morning and evening."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Recite: 'O Allāh, Knower of the unseen and the seen, Creator of the heavens and the earth, Lord and Sovereign of all things. I bear witness that there is no deity worthy of worship except You. I seek refuge in You from the evil of my own self, from the evil of Shayṭān, and from his shirk (associating partners with You).' Recite this in the morning, in the evening, and when you go to sleep.""

*Al-Adab al-Mufrad, Hadith: 1208; Arabic Hadith: 1208*"
"1209","Abu Hurayra, may Allah be pleased with him, reported something similar to the previous hadith, in which the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, ""The Lord of everything and its Sovereign."" He also said, ""From the evil of Shaytan and his associates."""
